{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Shall remain alive.</b> From the heavy [intensive] conjugation [binyan hif'il], whose verbal noun is not mentioned. The yod ought to have been contracted with a vav [i.e., shureq], but it is lengthened on account of the guttural letter. Likewise יחרם כל רכושו." "<b>To make atonement upon it.</b> For the atonement shall be upon it, and its meaning is to send it away."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra references a supposed hif'il form with an unexpected long vowel before a guttural; the grammatical argument is compressed and assumes the reader knows the relevant forms."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:25.859521751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}